Helium shows as Ardia, and Helium's own services, update feed and crash server can't be reached.
Applied first in the series, on the tree 03-helium.py leaves (strings already renamed by ardia_namesub.py,
icons already replaced from ardia_resources.txt); it covers what those can't reach, literals in source:
- Helium's internal-page scheme alias is unregistered: the engine neither registers, rewrites nor shows it, and shows
  chrome:// as chrome:// (the app shows those as ardia:// and owns ardia:// itself, as before Helium);
- the crash product is Ardia, there is no crash upload URL and no switch to set one; the browser update feed is empty;
- Helium services are off for good: ShouldAccessServices is false whatever the prefs say, every services URL is
  an unresolvable placeholder, the settings row that opens them is gone and the page's input has no Helium host;
- extension update pings are enabled for no domain (they were for helium.computer);
- chrome://credits names Ardia and its source repository; Helium's GPL-3.0 licence entry stays in the list;
- chrome://crashes files bugs on Ardia's issue tracker; the Safari import dialog has no help link (it pointed at
  Helium's wiki);
- screenshots save as ardia_screenshot*.png; the Web Store's button says "Add to Ardia";
- chrome://flags: descriptions say Ardia, Helium's flag ids are ardia-*, and the updater channel and update server
  flags are gone (the app has its own updater), as are the Proxy server and Proxy bypass list flags (on a real profile
  ArdiaCore drops --proxy-server from the browser's command line, after chrome://flags apply);
- cr:chrome-product is Ardia's mark (traced from docs/brand/ardia/source/mark-small.png), as are the product
  vector icons and logos ardia_resources.txt copies in;
- Helium's indigo palette is undone (helium-color-scheme.patch reversed): chrome:// pages and dialogs use
  Chromium's colours, as Ardia does today;
- the onboarding page and Helium's uBlock Origin aren't packed or registered (Ardia has its own onboarding and its
  own uBlock Origin);
- chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING is Chromium's again (Ardia builds with chrome/app/theme/ardia/BRANDING).

